  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A parabola with equation \\(y = x^2 + bx + c\\) passes through the points \\((2, 3)\\) and \\((4, 3).\\) What is \\(c?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "11"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2006-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substituting the points gives \\(3 = 4 + 2b + c\\) and \\(3 = 16 + 4b + c.\\) Subtracting yields \\(0 = 12 + 2b,\\) so \\(b = -6.\\)\n\nThen \\(c = 3 - 4 - 2(-6) = 11.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The two points have the same \\(y\\)-value, so they are symmetric about the vertex",
        "The axis of symmetry is \\(x = 3,\\) giving \\(b = -6\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
